nodes.body:
Thanks for the review. On the P3 (heuristic pins in the tests): agreed. The expected-form column of `_FORM_CELLS` and the `SPARSE_DECODE_SPLIT_CAP == 16` assertion freeze measured winners, which `test/AGENTS.md`'s heuristic-test rule asks tests not to do. The fix lands in the follow-up stacked on this PR (the sparse core's `griddepcontrol` sites), so it carries its own Rubin run:

* the selector loop keeps only the one-source property -- the sparse pin equals the dense adapter's rule on the same `(B, H_q, S_q, split)` grid and device, for every cell -- which survives a refit of that rule's constants;
* adapter-to-compiler transport stays on the mocked chooser (`compile_ptr` recorded through a stub, as today);
* the Rubin numerical and census cells force each combine form explicitly instead of relying on a measured cell selecting it;
* the split-rule test asserts the legal bounds (`1 <= cap <= 17`, the tiles of a 512-list item; the fill rule monotone in the item count) instead of the constant's value, whose sweep provenance stays in the docstring.

Merging this PR on the GPU lane's verdict, as the review leaves the timing with the owner.

